cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use wormbench, please cite it as below, and cite the real-worm data it grades against (see the README)."
type: software
title: "wormbench: grading simulated and real C. elegans tracks against real-worm behaviour"
authors:
  - family-names: Zaharia
    given-names: Chris Julian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-6849-8081"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SyntheticBrains/nematode"
url: "https://github.com/SyntheticBrains/nematode/tree/main/packages/wormbench"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
keywords:
  - C. elegans
  - behaviour
  - benchmark
  - foraging
  - roaming and dwelling
  - local search
  - chemotaxis
abstract: >-
  A grader for simulated or real C. elegans tracks on standard assays: Scheer and
  Bargmann's small lawn and uniform well, the kinematics and activity of worms on a
  lawn, López-Cruz et al.'s local search after food removal, and Chen et al.'s
  butanone chemotaxis. Each statistic is graded against bands built from the spread
  between real recording dates, at the population's own size.
